[7.984,"o","$ "]
[7.985,"o","ov version\r\n"]
[8.02,"o","ov ov-admin\r\n"]
[8.195,"m","Deploy (--mode assisted): ov prints the commands and runs nothing"]
[8.195,"o","$ "]
[8.196,"o","ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-do-el-s111429 --cloud digitalocean --do-region \"$DO_REGION\" --edition pro --openvidu-pro-license \"$OPENVIDU_PRO_LICENSE\" --deployment-type elastic --certificate-type selfsigned --param fixedNumberOfMediaNodes=1 --mode assisted\r\n"]
[12.126,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[12.128,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nRun these commands yourself in your DigitalOcean account (region fra1, Spaces in fra1); ov runs none of them:\r\n\r\n  # Terraform authenticates with the token in the variables file (from DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN).\r\n  # Read before anything is created (reads only, with the API token): the region fra1 exists and takes new Droplets; the size s-4vcpu-8gb is offered in fra1; Droplets: 2 needed (the master and 1 media node), 25 free (limit 25, 0 in use).\r\n  # The same reads: curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN\" https://api.digitalocean.com/v2/account\r\n  #   curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN\" https://api.digitalocean.com/v2/droplets?per_page=1\r\n  #   curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN\" https://api.digitalocean.com/v2/sizes?per_page=200\r\n  #   curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN\" https://api.digitalocean.com/v2/regions?per_page=200\r\n  # The template, rendered from the one embedded in this CLI for the elastic topology,\r\n  # and its variables, written out for you to read (the variables file is 0600: it\r\n  # carries the license):\r\n  #   .openvidu/digitalocean/tf-do-openvidu-pro-elastic.tf\r\n  #   .openvidu/digitalocean/openvidu.auto.tfvars.json\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/digitalocean init -input=false -no-color -force-copy\r\n  # If this stack already exists, read first what the apply would change: a new script a Droplet\r\n  # boots with (the domain, the certificate, the license, the Meet credentials or another OpenVidu CLI) REPLACES\r\n  # that Droplet, which starts again from scratch, and Terraform's plan says \"must be replaced\":\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/digitalocean plan\r\n  # Create the machines. deployedBy=instance: master-1 installs OpenVidu with the\r\n  # OpenVidu CLI and the other nodes join it. `apply` returns when Terraform is done (about 1 minute, then OpenVidu installs).\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/digitalocean apply -auto-approve -input=false -no-color\r\n\r\n  # Read back where the stack is (sensitive outputs, such as a generated SSH key, show as\r\n  # <sensitive>: `terraform output -raw <name>` prints one).\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/digitalocean output\r\n  # What the stack published: URL, credentials and the stack's access in secrets.env, in the\r\n  # stack's Space (the access appears once OpenVidu is up: until then this read fails, and the command that continues the deploy waits for it). Read with the Spaces keys.\r\n  SPACE=\"$(terraform -chdir=.openvidu/digitalocean output -raw appDataBucket)\"\r\n  env AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=*** AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=*** AWS_SESSION_TOKEN= aws s3 cp s3://$SPACE/secrets.env - --endpoint-url https://fra1.digitaloceanspaces.com\r\n\r\nNothing above has been run. Once these commands have finished, run this same command again:\r\n\r\n  ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-do-el-s111429 --cloud digitalocean --mode assisted\r\n\r\nIt finds the machines, waits for OpenVidu to come up and registers this directory as the\r\nstack. It creates nothing in your account.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
[12.31,"m","The runbook's commands, exactly as ov printed them 1/6"]
